"To expand the product \\((x+1)^2 \\cdot x\\), we will follow these steps:\n\n1. Expand \\((x+1)^2\\).\n2. Multiply the result by \\(x\\).\n\nFirst, let's expand \\((x+1)^2\\):\n\n\\[\n(x+1)^2 = (x+1)(x+1)\n\\]\n\nUsing the distributive property (also known as the FOIL method for binomials):\n\n\\[\n(x+1)(x+1) = x \\cdot x + x \\cdot 1 + 1 \\cdot x + 1 \\cdot 1 = x^2 + x + x + 1 = x^2 + 2x + 1\n\\]\n\nNext, we multiply this result by \\(x\\):\n\n\\[\n(x^2 + 2x + 1) \\cdot x = x^3 + 2x^2 + x\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the expanded form of the product \\((x + 1^2) \\cdot x\\) is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{x^3 + 2x^2 + x}\n\\]"
