"To solve the equation \\(\\sqrt{400} = \\sqrt{81} + \\sqrt{n}\\), we start by simplifying the square roots on both sides.\n\nFirst, simplify \\(\\sqrt{400}\\):\n\\[\n\\sqrt{400} = 20\n\\]\n\nNext, simplify \\(\\sqrt{81}\\):\n\\[\n\\sqrt{81} = 9\n\\]\n\nNow substitute these values back into the equation:\n\\[\n20 = 9 + \\sqrt{n}\n\\]\n\nTo isolate \\(\\sqrt{n}\\), subtract 9 from both sides:\n\\[\n20 - 9 = \\sqrt{n}\n\\]\n\\[\n11 = \\sqrt{n}\n\\]\n\nTo solve for \\(n\\), square both sides of the equation:\n\\[\n11^2 = (\\sqrt{n})^2\n\\]\n\\[\n121 = n\n\\]\n\nThus, the value of \\(n\\) is \\(\\boxed{121}\\)."
