"Let \\( d \\) be the number of dimes and \\( n \\) be the number of nickels. We have two equations based on the given information:\n\n1. \\( d + n = 11 \\)\n2. \\( 10d + 5n = 75 \\)\n\nFirst, we solve the first equation for \\( d \\):\n\\[ d = 11 - n \\]\n\nNext, we substitute \\( d = 11 - n \\) into the second equation:\n\\[ 10(11 - n) + 5n = 75 \\]\n\\[ 110 - 10n + 5n = 75 \\]\n\\[ 110 - 5n = 75 \\]\n\\[ 110 - 75 = 5n \\]\n\\[ 35 = 5n \\]\n\\[ n = \\frac{35}{5} \\]\n\\[ n = 7 \\]\n\nTherefore, Hillary has 7 nickels. The final answer is \\( \\boxed{7} \\).\n\nFinal Answer: The final answer is $7$. I hope it is correct."
"To solve the inequality \\(-4 < 2(x - 1) < 8\\), we first isolate the middle term \\(2(x - 1)\\):\n\n\\[-4 < 2(x - 1) < 8\\]\n\nDivide all parts of the inequality by 2:\n\n\\[ \\frac{-4}{2} < \\frac{2(x - 1)}{2} < \\frac{8}{2} \\]\n\nThis simplifies to:\n\n\\[ -2 < x - 1 < 4 \\]\n\nNext, add 1 to all parts of the inequality to solve for \\(x\\):\n\n\\[ -2 + 1 < x - 1 + 1 < 4 + 1 \\]\n\nThis simplifies to:\n\n\\[ -1 < x < 5 \\]\n\nSo, the solution to the inequality is \\(-1 < x < 5\\). Here, \\(a = -1\\) and \\(b = 5\\).\n\nTherefore, \\(a + b\\) is:\n\n\\[ a + b = -1 + 5 = 4 \\]\n\nThe final answer is \\(\\boxed{4}\\)."
