"To determine the probability that Harold gets at least as many heads as tails when tosses a nickel four times, we need to consider the possible outcomes and count the favorable ones.\n\nFirst, let's list the possible outcomes of tossing a nickel four times:\n1. HHHH\n2. HHHT\n3. HHTH\n4. HHTT\n5. THHH\n6. THHT\n7. TTTH\n8. TTTT\n\nThere are 8 possible outcomes in total.\n\nNext, we need to count the favorable outcomes where the number of heads is at least as many as the number of tails. These outcomes are:\n1. HHHH\n2. HHHT\n3. HHTH\n4. THHH\n5. THHT\n6. TTTH\n\nThere are 6 favorable outcomes.\n\nThe probability of an event is given by the ratio of the number of favorable outcomes to the total number of possible outcomes. Therefore, the probability that Harold gets at least as many heads as tails is:\n$$ \\frac{6}{8} = \\frac{3}{4} $$\n\nThe final answer is $\\frac{3}{4}$. I hope it is correct."
