"The volume of a sphere is given by the formula \\( V = \\frac{4}{3}\\pi r^3 \\).\n\nFirst, calculate the volume of one small sphere:\n\\[ V_{\\text{small}} = \\frac{4}{3}\\pi (3)^3 = \\frac{4}{3}\\pi \\cdot 27 = 36\\pi \\]\n\nSince there are 27 small spheres, the total volume is:\n\\[ V_{\\text{total}} = 27 \\times 36\\pi = 972\\pi \\]\n\nLet \\( R \\) be the radius of the larger sphere. The volume of the larger sphere is:\n\\[ V_{\\text{large}} = \\frac{4}{3}\\pi R^3 = 972\\pi \\]\n\nDivide both sides by \\( \\frac{4}{3}\\pi \\):\n\\[ R^3 = 972 \\]\n\nTake the cube root of both sides to solve for \\( R \\):\n\\[ R = \\sqrt[3]{972} = 9 \\]\n\nTherefore, the radius of the larger sphere is \\( \\boxed{9} \\)."
