"To find the positive difference between the greatest and least prime factors of 2000, we first need to determine the prime factorization of 2000.\n\n1. Divide 2000 by the smallest prime number, which is 2:\n   \\[\n   2000 \\div 2 = 1000\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   1000 \\div 2 = 500\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   500 \\div 2 = 250\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   250 \\div 2 = 125\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   125 \\div 5 = 5\n   \\]\n\nSo, the prime factorization of 2000 is \\(2^4 \\times 5^3\\).\n\nThe least prime factor is 2, and the greatest prime factor is 5.\n\nNow, we calculate the positive difference between the greatest and least prime factors:\n\\[\n5 - 2 = 3\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the final answer is \\(\\boxed{3}\\)."
