"To find the length of the common side of the rectangular garden, we start by using the formula for the area of a rectangle, which is given by:\n\n\\[ \\text{Area} = \\text{length} \\times \\text{width} \\]\n\nIn this problem, the area of the garden is 184 square feet, and one side (the width) is 8 feet. We need to find the length of the other side (the length). Let's denote the length of the common side by \\( L \\).\n\nUsing the area formula, we have:\n\n\\[ 184 = L \\times 8 \\]\n\nTo find \\( L \\), we solve for \\( L \\) by dividing both sides of the equation by 8:\n\n\\[ L = \\frac{184}{8} \\]\n\n\\[ L = 23 \\]\n\nTherefore, the length of the common side is \\(\\boxed{23}\\) feet."
