"To determine the average of the integers $71, 72, 73, 74, 75$, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Add all the integers together.\n2. Divide the sum by the number of integers.\n\nFirst, let's add the integers:\n\n\\[\n71 + 72 + 73 + 74 + 75\n\\]\n\nAdding these together:\n\n\\[\n71 + 72 = 143\n\\]\n\\[\n143 + 73 = 216\n\\]\n\\[\n216 + 74 = 290\n\\]\n\\[\n290 + 75 = 365\n\\]\n\nSo, the sum of the integers is $365$.\n\nNext, we divide the sum by the number of integers, which is $5$:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{365}{5} = 73\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the average of the integers is $\\boxed{73}$.\n\nFinal Answer:\nThe final answer is $\\boxed{73}$. I hope it is correct."
